    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51729" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθείμαρται</span></b> , pf.
		
			Pass.
		, used impers., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>it is
				ordained by fate</i>, esp. to one's ruin, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Philopatr.</u>
				14
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span> c.inf., ib.<i><span class="en">
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Epict.</u>
				2.6.10
			</span></i>: plpf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθείμαρτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chrysipp.Stoic.
					2.292
				</span></i>
			; also pers., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βραχὺς χρόνος ὁ τοῦ ζῆν ἑκάστῳ
					καθείμαρται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Am.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			; part., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάλαι
				καθειμαρμένων τούτων</span>
			<i>having been ordained by fate</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Alex.</u>
				52
			</span></i>.</div>
